 { Erdos – Sutovsky, Gibraltar 2012 } { _ } 29... { -KEY- } fxg6 $3 { Chess is a game and it has to be played. This is easy to forget when we analyse with our computers. Most decisions in a chess game will be the solution of minor problems, not related to winning or losing the game, but to getting the best chances of going in that direction. The method of comparison is very useful in this case as well. } ( 29... hxg6 $6 { is incorrect as it leads by force to an ending with opposite-coloured bishops: } 30. Qf6 $1 ( 29... fxg6 29. Kxg2 Qe4 31. Qf3 c5 { is hopeless for White, the main reason being: } 32. Qxe4 Rxe4 33. Kf3 f5 $1 { -+ } ) 
